[E0404] Error: cannot copy `x`
   ╭─[ err/69_generic_moves/main.wip:6:28 ]
   │
 6 │ fn duplicate<T>(x: T): T = x
   │                            ┬
   │                            ╰── `x` has type `T`
   │
   │ Help: to transfer ownership, write `move x`
   │
   │ Note: a value that contains `own` has exactly one owner, so it is never copied
───╯
[E0405] Error: cannot copy `x`, which is behind a reference
    ╭─[ err/69_generic_moves/main.wip:10:16 ]
    │
 10 │         return x
    │                ┬
    │                ╰── a `for` binding, which refers to an element
    │
    │ Help: elements stay where they are while a loop walks them; to take one out, move the whole array
    │
    │ Note: a reference can read a value but cannot take ownership of it
────╯
[E0406] Error: cannot copy an array element that contains `own`
    ╭─[ err/69_generic_moves/main.wip:12:5 ]
    │
 12 │     xs[0]
    │     ──┬──
    │       ╰──── an element of an array
    │
    │ Note: taking one element would leave a hole in the array; an array of `own` values is moved as a whole
────╯
